ck" content="true" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:android:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:ios:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:web:url" content="https://www.meetup.com/" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:site" content="@meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:image" content="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/shared/meetup-flyer.png" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:description" content="Find Meetup events and groups so you can do more of what matters to you and meet people near you who share your interests." data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:iphone" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:iphone" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:ipad" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:ipad" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:googleplay" content="com.meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:googleplay" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" data-next-head=""/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.meetup.com/find/" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><script type="application/ld+json" data-next-head="">[{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Meet New People, Great Conversations & 50+ Board Games | 25–45 | Fast Friends ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-singles-in-the-city/events/316645540/","description":"Ever wish there were an easier way to turn a room full of strangers into people you actually want to talk to?\n*That’s what Fast Friends is designed for.*\n\nInstead of arriving at a busy pub and wondering who to approach, our host guides you through short conversations and rotations, giving you the chance to meet a variety of people throughout the evening. You get a little structure to make connecting easier — without making the evening feel forced or formal.\n\nAnd once the hosted rounds finish, you can keep the evening going. 🎲\nWe’re back at Stout Irish Pub in Cabbagetown — a relaxed Irish pub with food, drinks and 50+ board games, giving you plenty of ways to continue socialising with the people you’ve met.\n\n🎟️ Book Early & Save: [https://toronto17thoct.eventbrite.co.uk](https://toronto17thoct.eventbrite.co.uk)\nEarly Bird: CAD $10\nRegular: CAD $15\nAt the Door: CAD $20 cash — to host Faye\nBooking ahead helps us plan the right group size and venue space, and your ticket confirms your place.\n\n🤝 What to Expect\n7:00 PM — Welcome & Drinks\nMeet your host, Faye, grab a drink and settle in.\nComing alone? Completely fine. Many guests arrive solo, and we’ll help you get comfortable and connected from the start.\n7:30 PM — Fast Friends\nThis is where the evening gets going.\nYou’ll move through a series of short, guided conversations, meeting different people along the way. Our host keeps the rotations moving, so you don’t have to worry about who to approach or what to do next.\nJust show up, join the conversation and see who you click with.\n\n✨ Themed Connection Rounds\nThroughout the evening, we’ll mix in themed rounds and interactive prompts designed to make connecting easier.\nThey’ll help you discover shared interests, experiences and unexpected things you have in common — taking the conversation beyond the usual small talk.\n\n🎲 8:30 PM onwards — Board Games & Socialising\nOnce the hosted rounds finish, the evening doesn’t have to.\nStout has 50+ board games available, making it easy to keep the conversations going. Pick a game with the people you’ve met, grab another drink, join a group or simply continue chatting.\nYou don’t have to be a serious gamer — the games are simply another easy way to socialise and get to know people.\n\n🍻 Staying Later?\nStout’s current After Dark Special runs from 9–11 PM, with $7 beers and $7 highballs, among other specials.\n\n❤️ Why Come Along?\n✔️ Meet 15–25 new people in one evening\n✔️ Guided conversations make meeting people easier\n✔️ Meet different people through rotating conversations\n✔️ Interactive themed rounds to spark better conversations\n✔️ 50+ board games available afterwards 🎲\n✔️ Relaxed Irish pub atmosphere\n✔️ Reserved space for our group\n✔️ Most guests come solo\n✔️ Plenty of time to keep socialising after the hosted rounds\n✔️ Friendship-focused — not a dating event\n\n👋 Who Is It For?\nAges 25–45\nWhether you’ve just moved to Toronto, have lived here for years, or simply feel like your social circle could use some fresh faces, you’re welcome.\nYou don’t need to know anyone beforehand or arrive with a group.\nCome by yourself, bring a friend, or simply come ready to have a few good conversations and see where the evening takes you.\n\n🌍 About Fast Friends\nFor over 10 years, Fast Friends has been bringing people together through professionally hosted social events in 30+ cities worldwide.\nOur goal is simple: make meeting new people easier, more relaxed and more enjoyable.\nCome for the conversations. Stay for the games. Leave with new connections. ❤️","startDate":"2026-10-17T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Stout Irish pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"221 Carlton St., Toronto, ON M5A 2L2, Canada,, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Singles in the city (13000+)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-singles-in-the-city/"},"performer":"Toronto Singles in the city (13000+)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Fall Colours Canoe trip to Kawartha Highlands Provincial Park","url":"https://www.meetup.com/gta-vibe-and-wander-com/events/316562323/","description":"This is a trip to view the back country Ontario during prime fall colours.\n\nThis is a one-night trip. We will paddle into the interior and camp for the night.\nThere are 2 small portage.\n\nCamp sites and canoes will be reserved. Food will be provided and carpooling arranged. You do not need to bring any food.\n\nWe will be asking for a $50 deposit via paypal or bank email transfer to keep your spot since I need to reserve the sites and canoes ahead of time. I will send out a note with further information to those who sign up. See paypal and bank email transfer info under \"COSTS\" below.\nRSVP REQUIREMENTS\n\nRSVP \"Going\" if you are sure you can attend, are able to meet the difficulty requirement, bring what is needed and have reviewed the costs associated with this event.\nEVENT DETAILS\nDifficulty: Easy to Moderate - You are able to paddle 3-4 hours per day and are reasonably fit.\n\nWhat to Bring:\nHat, Personal water bottle, 2 or 3 dry bags or garbage bags (to use for your clothes & sleeping bag) Put the garbage bag inside to line you backpack. Put another one inside your sleeping bag case to line that.\nWaterproof Coat.\nList of Clothing : Hat, swimsuit, sweaters or sweatshirts (it will get cold in the evenings), jeans or long pants, 1 towel, 2 pairs shoes - 1 for dry hiking and 1 for wet stuff. Wet shoes need to be secure, flip flops and loose sandals may get stuck in the mud.\nbowl, cup, spoon, fork, sun glasses, flashlight or strong headlamp,\nToiletries: Toilet paper, sunscreen, bug spray.\nWhen you pack your stuff, if you can pack everything in one pack, portaging will be much easier!\nOther camping items:\nBackpack, Sleeping bag (suitable for cold weather), sleeping pad or mattress\n\nGETTING THERE\nDrivers will be notified by the organizer where to meet and pick up passengers. Drivers will be sent complete directions as to where, when and who to meet and directions to the Park.\nPlease sign up for the carpool here:\n\nCOSTS\nOther: 50 deposit to remain on going list. Total cost between 180 and $220. This cost includes all gas, camp fees, food and canoe rentals. The balance is payable at the end of the trip when we calculate the costs owed by each member.\nHOW TO PAY: contact Pedro for paypal account and e-mail address\nINTRODUCTION TO CANOEING\nPlease review the following safety videos:\n(You don't need to kneel, sitting is fine for this type of trip. The other safety tips are good)\n[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PrjXT9bAB6c](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PrjXT9bAB6c)\n[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sTtFSpelQk4](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sTtFSpelQk4)\n[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_zHSfEhEqkU](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_zHSfEhEqkU)\nPlease ALWAYS check your email or the event post in the evening or in the morning prior to the event for cancellation, rescheduling or last minute changes.\nPlease Note: You are required to respond to Meetup messages in a timely manner. The messages may be on the comment board below, private message, or through the email address you have registered with [Meetup.com.](http://Meetup.com.)","startDate":"2026-10-17T11:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addres