Only registered members can participate; visitors are not permitted. If you wish to participate, please register as a member first, and then view the event details and participation instructions.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* ⚠️⚠️⚠️\nTo ensure efficient use of event slots and fairness, all registered participants must confirm their attendance with the group administrator before the specified deadline (if a waitlist exists). \\* Before the deadline, registered members have the right to cancel and priority. To ensure fairness, if no response is received after the deadline, the waiting list member has priority.\n\nIf you do not confirm your attendance within 72 hours before the event, or are absent, your slot may be reassigned to a waiting list candidate or a new member. This rule aims to ensure fairness and maximize the participation opportunities for all members. Since the venue cost is shared by all confirmed participants, 🛎️ those who do not attend must notify the administrator before the deadline. Failure to notify the administrator before the deadline will result in payment of the venue cost. Thank you for your understanding. \\*Please note: Failure to pay the venue cost will result in your cancellation of membership.\n\nSlot allocation is based on the order of candidate responses. To ensure fairness and better coordination, when a registered candidate cancels their slot, the administrator will send a separate notification to all candidates each time slots open. Due to limited availability, places will be allocated on a first-come, first-served basis based on response time.\n\n\\*If you need to cancel your participation, please notify the administrator at least 24 hours before the event. Late cancellations will incur venue fees. Thank you for your understanding and cooperation.\n\n\\*To ensure fairness and transparency, each participant needs to confirm individually. Members who fail to cancel their registration and complete payment within the specified time will be permanently disqualified.\n\nPlease note that if you confirm participation on behalf of another member, you will be responsible for that member's event costs.\n\nTo maintain fairness for all participants, please inform your friends that they must also confirm.\n\n\\*In the event of repeated violations, the administrator reserves the right to make the final decision.\n\nThank you for your understanding and cooperation.\n\n* After reading the event details, members can contact the administrator via message.","startDate":"2026-10-17T13:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"CA Badminton Academy","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Scarborough","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1370 Birchmount rd, unit 6, Scarborough, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"CA Badminton Meetup Toronto Group GTA","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ca-badminton-meetup-toronto-group-gta/"},"performer":"CA Badminton Meetup Toronto Group GTA"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🐾 Give Back: TNR Cat Rescue Volunteer Day","url":"https://www.meetup.com/gta-vibe-and-wander-com/events/316773261/","description":"Please read the details before RSVPing.\n\n🐾 Time to give back, guys\n\nWe’ve partnered with a non-profit animal rescue group to support a TNR (Trap-Neuter-Return) campaign in Scarborough, near 75 Birchmount Ave.\n\nWe’re looking for volunteers to help with\n\n1. 🪤 Setting up traps at designated locations\n2. 🚗 Transporting cats to/from the clinic\n3. 🐱 Feeding cats at designated locations\n\nSome activities require access to your own vehicle, while others simply require your time and willingness to help.\n\nEvery little bit helps, and the cats definitely need us. ❤️?\n\nAnyone allergic to cats, furs or anything related to animals, please do not signup\n\nYou participate this in this event at your own risk. Organizers of this meetup or anyone who is part of this campaign isn't responsible for any untoward incident during your participation in this event .","startDate":"2026-10-17T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Scarborough Gardens Arena","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Scarborough","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"75 Birchmount Road, Scarborough, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Vibe & Wander","url":"https://www.meetup.com/gta-vibe-and-wander-com/"},"performer":"Vibe & Wander"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Singles Dance Party @ The Oasis","url":"https://www.meetup.com/singlespartiescom/events/316683759/","description":"Singles Dance Party + 40 crowd\nSaturday October 17th 7:30 start\n**The Oasis Convention Centre**\n1036 Lakeshore Rd East. Mississauga\nHuge Dance Floor\n**Dance The Night Away**\nJoin us for an exciting evening of socializing, mingling, and connecting\nwith other singles in your area. Whether you're new in town, looking for a potential partner, or simply want to meet like-minded people, this event is perfect for you. An opportunity to expand your social circle and have a great time in a relaxed and friendly atmosphere.\nThe cost is $20.00. Get your tickets at the door\nFor more info call 416-236-8222.\nSee you there!","startDate":"2026-10-17T23:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Oasis Convention Centre","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1036 Lakeshore Rd E, Mississauga, ON L5E 1E4, Canada, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"SinglesParties.com","url":"https://www.meetup.com/singlespartiescom/"},"performer":"SinglesParties.com"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🎃🍂 PUMPKINS AFTER DARK – MARKHAM ROAD TRIP! 🍂🎃","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316732524/","description":"🎃🍂 PUMPKINS AFTER DARK – MARKHAM ROAD TRIP! 🍂🎃\nSaturday, October 17\n\nLooking for the perfect pre-Halloween/Fall activity? One of our group members, Emma, suggested this cool idea — so we're heading out to Pumpkins After Dark in Markham! 🎃✨\n\nThis will be the FIRST TIME our Meetup group has done Pumpkins After Dark, and it looks like a fantastic way to get into the Halloween spirit!\n\n🌙 THE PLAN\n\nWe'll meet at 8:00 PM outside Christie Station and then head to Markham together in a rental SUV.\n\nThe road trip transportation includes:\n\n🚙 Round-trip transportation from Toronto\n🎃 Transportation to and from Pumpkins After Dark\n👻 A fun evening with the group\n🍂 A perfect Fall/pre-Halloween night out!\n\n💰 TRANSPORTATION: $25\n\nThe $25 covers your round-trip transportation only.\n\n⚠️ IMPORTANT: Your Pumpkins After Dark admission ticket is NOT included. You must purchase your own event admission separately.\n\n🎟️ Buy your Pumpkins After Dark ticket here:\n\nhttps://pumpkinsafterdark.com/markham\n\n🚨 RESERVE YOUR SPOT\n\nBecause we're using a rental SUV with limited space, your spot is NOT locked in until I receive your $25 e-transfer.\n\n📧 E-transfer: nicolasbello@yahoo.com\n💵 $25 per person\n\nPlease don't RSVP unless you're committed to coming and can send the $25 to secure your spot.\n\n🎃 WHY THIS WILL BE FUN\n\nThink giant glowing pumpkins, Halloween displays, crisp Fall weather, music, photos and a bunch of friends enjoying one of the most seasonal activities around.\n\nIt's basically the perfect excuse to start celebrating Halloween before Halloween actually arrives! 👻🍂\n\nCome for the pumpkins, stay for the road-trip fun!\n\nFirst time for our group — let's make it a good one! 🎃🚙","startDate":"2026-10-18T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Christie Station","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Bloor and Christie, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"The Saturday Autumn Colours Ashbridges Bay- Walk, Talk and Good Times! ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/events/316611635/","description":"Hello everyone,\n\n\\*Please read carefully\\*\n\nLooking to enjoy the beautiful colours of autumn, have some great conversations and meet new people? Join us for a relaxed Saturday walk through Ashbridges Bay! We’ll take in the waterfront scenery, enjoy the fresh air and create plenty of opportunities to talk, laugh and make new friends along the way. Come by yourself or bring a friend—either way, you’ll receive a warm welcome!\n\n\\*Joined by my other groups too :)\n\n**Arrive between 2:30 pm and 3:00 pm**\n\n**Where to meet us:**\n\nMeetup us outside **Woodbine Station beside bike racks**\n**The Main Woodbine Station Entrance:** Located at the southeast corner of Woodbine Avenue and Strathmore Boulevard.\n\nWe will walk as a group from the station down to Ashbridges Bay\n\\*Most will stick around after for a bite to eat, ice cream and/or a beverage to sip on :)\n\nFurther details below:\n\nSincerely,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n\n**Event Details:**\n**The Saturday Autumn Colours Ashbridges Bay- Walk, Talk and Good Times!**\n\nWhat to expect:\n\n* A relaxed walk along the Ashbridges Bay waterfront\n* Ice breaker games to get to know one another\n* Plenty of opportunities to mix, mingle and meet new people\n* A comfortable pace that allows everyone to walk and talk\n* Beautiful views of the lake, beach, parkland and surrounding area\n* A positive atmosphere for both newcomers and returning members\n\nPlease wear comfortable walking shoes and bring water, sunscreen or anything else you may need for the weather. The purpose of this event is simple: get outside, enjoy the day and make a few new connections!\n\\* Many of us will hit a local pub/restaurant after the walk for dinner and beverages- plan to join us for that if you can\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**Event Fee:**\n10 dollars (cash only) when you arrive (HST is included)\nor e transfer in advance to [Steveflemming11@gmail.com](mailto:Steveflemming11@gmail.com)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n\nParking near Woodbine Station:\n(Although I encourage you to take subway if you can)","startDate":"2026-10-17T19:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Woodbine Subway Station","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"991 Woodbine Avenue, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/"},"performer":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Volition Street Smart Tour: One Toronto Lot. Four Homes. Four OWNERS.","url":"https://www.meetup.com/volition/events/316765032/","description":"### **Tour a Real-World Toronto Condominiumization Project**\n\nWhat if, instead of building a multiplex and renting out the units, you could **build multiple homes on a single Toronto lot and sell each one individually?**\n\nThat's the idea behind **condominiumization** – what we're calling the \"Missing Middle 2.0\" investment strategy – and for this Meetup, we're going to walk through a real project that's actually doing it.\n\nWhen most people hear the word \"condo,\" they probably picture one of two things: **a box in the sky, or a unit in a large stacked townhouse development.**\n\nThis is neither.\n\nWhat if you could create a \"condo\" that **looks and feels much more like a traditional home**? One with its own front door, multiple floors and the privacy and feel of a house – nestled discreetly into an established residential neighbourhood rather than looking like an obvious townhouse development?\n\n**That's what Harvie is creating.**\n\nThe Harvie project started with a single-family property. Today, it's being transformed into **three townhouse-style homes plus a garden suite**, each designed to be separately titled and sold individually.\n\nMost missing-middle investment strategies (like the well-known \"4+1\") follow essentially the same playbook:\n**Buy a property. Add units. Rent them out. Hold.**\n\nHarvie asks a different question:\n**What if the target customer wasn't four tenants... but four HOMEOWNERS?**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\n\n### **A Different Kind of Missing Middle**\n\nWe've spent a lot of time at Volition talking about Toronto's changing housing rules and the opportunities they create for small investors and developers. But almost all of that conversation has focused on **creating more rental housing**.\n\nCondominiumization introduces another possibility:\n**Creating more ownership housing.**\n\nFor many aspiring homeowners, there's a gap between the two traditional choices.\n\nOn one side is the **traditional house** – your own front door, multiple floors, privacy and the experience of living in an established residential neighbourhood – but increasingly at a price many aspiring homeowners simply can't afford.\n\nOn the other is the more attainable **condo apartment or stacked townhouse** – which may fit the budget better, but may not deliver the kind of home or lifestyle they're actually aspiring to own.\n\n**But what if there were something in between?**\n\nA home with its own front door. Multiple floors. More privacy. A residential streetscape. A home that feels like a real home, in a real neighbourhood – but on a smaller footprint and potentially at a more attainable price point than a traditional detached or semi-detached house.\n\n**That's the homebuyer Harvie is designed for.**\n\nWe're not just talking about adding density. We're talking about potentially creating **a type of ownership housing that sits between the condo apartment and the traditional Toronto house.**\n\nThat's what makes this \"Missing Middle 2.0\" concept so interesting.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\n\n### **From One Single-Family Property to Four Individually Owned Homes**\n\nThe concept sounds simple:\n**Take one Toronto residential property. Redevelop it into multiple family-sized homes. Condominiumize the property. Sell each home separately.**\n\nBut here's the critical difference:\n**You can't simply design the same rental multiplex you would have built for four tenants and decide afterward that you're going to sell the units individually.**\n\n**The end product has to be something a homeowner actually wants to BUY.**\n\nDifferent customer. Different product. Different design. Different economics.\n\nThat changes everything from the site you choose and the layout of the building to privacy, sound separation, construction quality, materials, finishes and how the individual homes actually function day-to-day.\n\nAnd rather than explain all of that with slides in a conference room:\n**We're taking you directly inside the Harvie project.**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\n\n### **What We'll Explore**\n\nUsing Harvie as our real-world case study, we'll dig into the questions that actually matter if you're considering this strategy:\n\n* **How does condominiumization actually work?** How do you go from one Toronto property to multiple separately titled homes that can ultimately be sold to individual homeowners?\n* **What makes a property a good candidate?** We'll look at how site dimensions, neighbourhood, comparable sales, acquisition costs and the potential value of the finished homes factor into choosing the right project.\n* **What do you build when your customer is a HOMEOWNER instead of a tenant?** We'll explore the design decisions behind Harvie's vertical townhouse-style homes, including layouts, privacy, sound separation, utilities and the details that make a unit actually feel like a home.\n* **What does it take to get a project like this approved and built?** We'll unpack some of the municipal, planning, design and construction challenges encountered along the way – while seeing the actual materials, construction methods and finished product firsthand.\n* **Does the business model actually work?** We'll explore the economics, financing and exit strategy, and how developing homes for individual sale changes the equation compared with building and holding a conventional rental multiplex.\n* And perhaps most importantly, **what do you only learn by actually doing it?** We'll get into the real-world challenges, surprises and lessons from executing the strategy – including what might be done differently on the next project.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\n\n### **Hear Directly From the Developer Behind Harvie**\n\nOur expert guest speaker **Daniel Zimberoff** is the investor and developer behind Harvie. He'll take us through the actual project firsthand – why it was designed this way, how the strategy was executed, what happened along the way and what he's learned from bringing it to reality.\n\nDan also runs a consulting practice **teaching other investors and developers how to execute condominiumization projects of their own.**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\n\n### **Come See the Real Thing**\n\nThis isn't a hypothetical pro forma.\nIt isn't a rendering.\nAnd it isn't a seminar about what *might* be possible.\n\n**We're going to walk through the real thing.**\n\n**One Toronto lot. Four homes. Four OWNERS.**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\n\n***\n\n**Schedule:**\nSaturday, October 17, 2026, 1:00-3:00 pm\n\n**Location:**\n534 Harvie Ave, Toronto, ON\n*(Limited street parking available. A short walk from the Eglinton Crosstown LRT - Fairbank and Caledonia stations)*\n\n***\n\n**Volition Properties:**\n\n*Make smarter real estate moves — buy, sell, or invest with confidence. Volition Properties offers tailored advice, education, and community — grounded in strategy, built on trust.*\n\nContact us today for any questions about real estate in Toronto!\n📧 info@volitionprop.com\n🌐 [www.volitionprop.com](https://www.volitionprop.com \"https://www.volitionprop.com\")\n📞 1-877-416-BRRR","startDate":"2026-10-17T17:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"534 Harvie Avenue","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"534 Harvie Ave, York, ON M6E 4M1, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"✪ TORONTO REAL ESTATE INVESTOR MASTERMIND ✪","url":"https://www.meetup.com/volition/"},"performer":"✪ TORONTO REAL ESTATE INVESTOR MASTERMIND ✪"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Queer Gayme Dive","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-gaymers/events/313122969/","description":"This is an opportunity to meet up for some LGBTQ2IA-flavoured gaming and socializing—allies also welcome. Come for the gaming, socializing, and the drinks! :) Be sure to invite friends and such, too. We’ll be in the larger area towards the back.\n\nEvent officially runs from 4pm to 7pm, at which point we start to pack away the games, clearing up before the band takes the stage (9:30-10pm).\n\nYou'll have access to a robust library of board games, and attendees are welcome to bring their own games.\n\nThere is no event fee. Instead we ask attendees to purchase beverages from the venue, Penny's Bar, conveniently located beside Lansdowne subway station at 1306 Bloor St. West. Of course, since they are offering us their space for free, please consider buying a drink if you can--possibly from our \\*custom menu\\*!\n\nWe provide nametag stickers with a pronoun field; we want this to be a comfortable environment for everyone, kindly respect people's listed or stated pronouns.\n\nIf you are unsure of someone's pronouns, don't assume: Ask, Respect and Practice\n\nDefinitely ask before taking pictures/videos\n\nAlas Penny's is not accessible due to stairs, dim lighting, and loud noises. While external food is welcome, outside beverages are not permitted.\n\\*\\*\\*Please reach out to [info@torontogaymers.ca](mailto:info@torontogaymers.ca) with any accessibility concerns.\n[https://linktr.ee/TorontoGaymers](https://linktr.ee/TorontoGaymers)\n\n#TorontoGaymers #PennysDiveBar [#Boardgames](https://keep.google.com/#label/boardgames)","startDate":"2026-10-17T20:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Penny's","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1306 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Gaymers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-gaymers/"},"performer":"Toronto Gaymers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🎬Movie: Street Fighter -  Food & Drinks after the movie 🍿!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316155672/","description":"🎬 Let’s Go to the Movies (and Actually Talk… or Not)\n\nWhether you're a film nerd, popcorn enthusiast, or just looking for a chill night out with interesting people — this one's for you.\n\nWe’re heading out to see a movie together, then grabbing food or drinks after. If the film's great (or terrible), we’ll probably talk about it forever. If it’s just okay, we’ll talk about it for 10 minutes and move on to everything else — books, dating apps, weird dreams, how Toronto keeps getting more expensive, etc.\n\nThe vibe is relaxed, friendly, and not too serious. No film degree needed. No icebreakers. No pressure to “perform.” Just come enjoy the film, connect with some thoughtful people, and see where the night goes Click here to watch trailer!\n\n🎞️ **Movie Title + Trailer:**[ \\[Click here to watch trailer!\\]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xt4X4FvXk2A&t=5s)\n\n📖 **📖 Plot Summary:** Set in 1993, estranged Street Fighters Ryu (Andrew Koji) and Ken Masters (Noah Centineo) are thrown back into combat when the mysterious Chun-Li (Callina Liang) recruits them for the next World Warrior Tournament: a brutal clash of fists, fate, and fury. But behind this battle royale lies a deadly conspiracy that forces them to face off against each other and the demons of their past. And if they don’t, it’s GAME OVER!\n\n***\n\n### 🗓️ **Event Details**\n\n📍 **Meetup Time:** 6:00 PM (Final time + theatre announced Tuesday of event week)\n🎬 **Movie Start Time:** TBA\n⏱️ **Runtime:** TBA\n📌 **Meetup Spot:** To be confirmed (based on theatre)\n🎟️ **Cost:**\n\n* **$11.50** for *CineClub* members\n* **$16.00** regular admission\n👉 You are responsible for buying your own ticket.\n\n**🪑 Reserved Seating:**\nYou must buy your ticket *before* signing up. You'll be asked where you're sitting so we can all sit together! However, members are welcome to sit anywhere that works for them.\n🎫 Buy your ticket here: [https://www.cineplex.com](https://www.cineplex.com)\n📍🪑 **Where I will be sitting:**\n\n🍿 **After the Movie:**\nYes, we’re heading out after! It’s not just a movie night — it’s a social night. Let's talk, laugh, and dissect every plot twist.\n\n***\n\n### ✅ **Before You Sign Up**\n\n* Please **buy your ticket first** — seating is limited!\n* When signing up, let us know your **seat number** so we can try to group everyone together.\n* You can still sign up or just **show up on the day** if you’re not sure you can make it — we’re flexible!\n\n📲 **Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[ Click here to join](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)\n🎟️ **Join Cineplex’s CineClub for discounts**: [https://www.cineplex.com/cineclub](https://www.cineplex.com/cineclub)\n🎁 **Get your SCENE Card** for free movies and points: [https://www.scene.ca](https://www.scene.ca)\n\n***\n\n### 🎥 **A Quick Word About Movie Etiquette**\n\nWe love a great film experience. Please:\n\n* Turn off your phone\n* Don’t talk during the movie\n* Be respectful of others\n\nRepeat offenders will be removed from the group — we take our cinema seriously (but with snacks).\n\n***\n\n### 👥 **About the Group**\n\nThis event is open to everyone — single, not single, shy, social, new in town or a long-time local. We're a group for people who love movies *and* making real connections. We also do walks, hikes, restaurants, arts & culture — come be part of it!\n🎬 **Organized by:** Mathew\n📧 Questions? Reach out: **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**","startDate":"2026-10-17T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@t